# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Table Mountain POV - ignored paths
#
# Rationale: this repo holds a 2.3 GB working set, almost all of it source or
# derived geospatial binaries. None of it belongs in git history. What IS
# tracked is the reproducible definition of the project: docs, scripts, the
# QGIS project, READMEs, and the small boundary layers the project references.
#
# Every ignored path below is regenerable. See docs/ for provenance.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Python environment and tooling ---------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- SQLite WAL journal sidecars ------------------------------------------
# Opening a GeoPackage in QGIS (or any SQLite client) can leave -wal/-shm
# companions or touch the header; the database content is the source of truth.
*.gpkg-wal
*.gpkg-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# --- Editor / OS noise ----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- OSM source and extracts ----------------------------------------------
# Permitted South Africa source extract and the park clip. Regenerate with the
# osmium command recorded in docs/osm_pbf_inspection.md. OSM data is ODbL and
# requires attribution; data/README.md carries it and stays tracked.
data/osm/*.pbf
data/osm/*.pbf.md5sum

# --- COCT source archives -------------------------------------------------
# 753 MB original download, retained unchanged on disk but not in git.
*.zip

# --- Large COCT / derived vector data -------------------------------------
# ~1 GB 2 m contour shapefile, extracted from the archive above.
# Excludes the directory CONTENTS, not the directory itself. Git does not
# descend into a wholly excluded directory, so naming the directory here would
# make the !**/README.md guard at the bottom of this file ineffective.
data/vector/coct/ground_level_map_2m_contours/*
# 420 MB bound-clipped 2 m contours, derived from the shapefile above by
# reprojecting ESRI:102562 -> EPSG:32734 and clipping to qgis/bound.shp.
data/vector/coct/contours_2m_within_bound.gpkg
# 50 MB OSM GeoPackage, regenerated by the ogr2ogr command in
# scripts/duckdb/README.md.
data/vector/table-mountain-national-park.gpkg

# --- Generated imagery derivatives ----------------------------------------
# Orthophoto exports and texture bakes. All large and reproducible; the
# regeneration command lives in data/imagery/README.md.
# NOTE: there is no data/terrain/ ignore rule. The COCT WMS "DTM" layers serve a
# hillshade render, not elevation, so nothing is stored there. Re-add a rule
# before writing any TIN/DEM product into data/terrain/.
data/imagery/*
!data/imagery/README.md

# --- Generated elevation derivatives --------------------------------------
# Continuous DEMs derived from the COCT contours; regenerate through the
# QGIS Processing workflow documented in data/elevation/README.md.
data/elevation/*.tif
!data/elevation/README.md

# --- Blender scene backups ------------------------------------------------
# Blender writes a .blend1 auto-backup beside each .blend on every save. These
# are regenerable by definition and were never intended to be tracked:
# table_mountain_pov.blend1 alone is 735 MB, and is an orphan - no
# table_mountain_pov.blend exists beside it.
blender/*.blend1

# NOTE: blender/*.blend is deliberately NOT ignored. The README treats scenes as
# build outputs, but scripts/blender/ does not exist, so the current .blend
# files are not reproducible from this repo. Track them until a build script
# exists; add an ignore rule at that point, not before.

# --- QGIS project save side-files -----------------------------------------
# QGIS >= 3.22 writes a <name>.qgs~ backup and a <name>_attachments.zip beside
# the project file on every GUI save. Neither is disableable and both are
# regenerable, so they are never committed; the tracked .qgs is always the
# build output (see qgis/README.md). The generic `*~` and `*.zip` rules above
# already matched these; the explicit rules document the intent.
*.qgs~
*_attachments.zip

# --- Render output --------------------------------------------------------
# Blender frames and videos.
renders/*
!renders/README.md

# --- Caches ---------------------------------------------------------------
cache/*
!cache/README.md

# --- Keep the provenance READMEs even inside ignored directories ----------
# Guards against a broad pattern above swallowing a data/README.md.
!**/README.md
